+### 2026-09-21 — RT-4 auto-reply boundary tested and hardened (Tarik)
+
+`tests/test_auto_reply_secret_egress.py` seeds a fake credential in a scratch
+environment, replaces the model call with adversarial output that repeats the
+credential exactly, and points all channel directories at a temporary tree.
+The test requires the run to refuse the reply before any draft is written and
+requires the canary to be absent from captured diagnostics. It then verifies
+that an ordinary reply still produces one draft.
+
+`channels/auto_reply.py` now rejects model output containing an exact,
+nontrivial value from a credential-like environment variable and redacts those
+values from model-call exception text. This is a narrow mechanical boundary,
+not a claim that prompt wording prevents exfiltration.
+
+**Limit:** this probe covers the autonomous email adapter only. It does not
+cover a shell-capable Goose session, `sessions.db`, worker transcripts, or a
+provider that has already received a secret through some other prompt path.
+
+**Next action (2026-09-22):** extend RT-4 to the shell-capable worker boundary:
+run a scratch Goose fixture with fake-only credentials, preserve its transcript,
+report and exception path, and assert that the canary is absent from all three
+and from the resulting patch. Do not expose a real provider credential.
